<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <%# Declared above the include, not below it: head.ejs writes the Twitter
     card from these two and a const declared after it is not in scope there.
     See the twitter:title comment in views/head.ejs. %>
  <% const title = '500 - Server Error - OldSchoolGames' %>
  <% const description = 'We encountered a server error. Please try again later or explore our collection of classic MS-DOS games.' %>
  <%- include('head', { title, description }) %>
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <meta name="description" content="<%= description %>" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="<%= title %>" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="<%= description %>" />
  <%# No og:url here, nor on the other three error views. Each of them named
      the site's address with its own status code on the end, and not one of
      those is an address on this site — nothing routes them, so a consumer
      that followed the tag was handed this same error page again.

      There is no honest value to put in its place. og:url is the canonical
      address of the thing being shared, and the thing being shared here is a
      failure: the address that was actually asked for is the one that does not
      work, and publishing it as canonical would be worse than saying nothing.
      With the tag gone a consumer falls back to the link it was given, which
      is the truth. The rest of the Open Graph block stays, so a shared link
      still gets a title, a description and a picture. %>
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="<%= siteName %>" />
  <%# Handed the title as head.ejs is — see the same line in views/404.ejs. %>
  <%- include('og-image', { title }) %>
</head>

<body class="layout">
  <%- include('navbar') %>
  <%- include('left-sidebar') %>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="text-xl" style="margin: 0 0 10px">500 &mdash; Something broke</h1>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 5px">
        Something went wrong on our side. The error has been logged &mdash;
        try again in a moment, or pick up somewhere else.
      </p>
      <%- include('error-nav') %>
    </div>
  </main>
  <%- include('right-sidebar') %>
  <%- include('footer') %>
</body>

</html>
